---
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro'

const facts = [
  { label: 'Language', value: 'Go, my daily driver' },
  { label: 'Focus', value: 'REST APIs & web systems' },
  { label: 'Based in', value: 'Jakarta, Indonesia' },
  { label: 'Currently', value: 'Open to backend roles' },
]
---

<section id="about" class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-24 sm:px-8">
  <SectionHeading title="I'm a builder who cares about the quiet details." />

  <div class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-5 md:gap-10">
    <div class="reveal md:col-span-3">
      <p class="mb-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-700">
        Hello, I'm Juanda, a backend developer with over a year of production experience in Go and
        CodeIgniter 4. I like my APIs honest, my schemas tidy, and my systems dependable: software that just
        works, predictably, under real use.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-700">
        My first real backend was a parish information system: I designed a MySQL schema with 10+ relational
        tables, built the CMS and admin dashboard on CodeIgniter 4, and cut content updates by 40% and data
        retrieval by 25% for staff across departments. I'm equally comfortable shaping React and Tailwind
        frontends, and I've shipped an API-backed Android app that folds a TensorFlow model into a real product.
        I've also run Study Jam workshops as a GDSC Curriculum Officer, so I can explain complex things to real
        people.
      </p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-ink-700">
        What I'm after is an entry-level backend role where I can grow my Go with senior engineers, building
        things that matter, doing them properly, and staying honest about what they are.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="reveal md:col-span-2">
      <div class="rounded-3xl border border-line bg-paper p-7">
        <p class="kicker mb-5">A few facts</p>
        <ul class="space-y-5 text-sm">
          {facts.map((f) => (
            <li class="flex flex-col gap-1">
              <span class="uppercase tracking-widest text-xs text-ink-500">{f.label}</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-ink-900">{f.value}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
